                <pb facs="0078" n="68" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg68"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/558: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castleman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-07T12:00:00-06:00">September 7,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. For Mr. Duggan. Referring to my telegram No. 97, September 6, 9 p.m.,
                    Honduran presentation of assurances took place at 11 with reported cordiality.
                    Shall report later regarding press handouts.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
